WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.450
November 1967. Britain
cuts the value of the pound

2
00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:07.700
from 2.80 dollars to 2.40.

3
00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:10.080
A cheaper currency.

4
00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:11.480
Good news for the country,

5
00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:12.880
or bad news?

6
00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:15.280
The trade figures did something odd.

7
00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:18.670
The current account
stayed in deficit in 1968,

8
00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:22.550
and only moved into surplus in 1969.

9
00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:25.570
So when a country's
money loses value abroad,

10
00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:28.250
who wins and who loses at home?

11
00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:31.750
In this mission, you'll follow
prices across the border,

12
00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:36.550
then see what happens to the whole
economy on an AD and AS diagram.

13
00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:39.200
Then you'll trace the
trade balance through time,

14
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:42.950
and find out why it can get
worse before it gets better.

15
00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:46.320
Your mission: find out
who gains and who pays

16
00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:47.880
when a currency falls.
